---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'How to report a concern about the OpenAR Collective under the Foundation Whistleblower Policy, and the protections that apply.';
---

<Base title="Report a Concern" description={description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <p class="overline">Whistleblower reporting</p>
      <h1>Report a concern</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Foundation wants to hear about conduct that may violate the law or a Foundation policy.
        Reports can come from anyone, including community participants, contributors, contractors,
        directors, officers, and members of the public.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="protection">
      <h2 id="protection">The protection</h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation prohibits retaliation against any person who makes a report in good faith or
        who participates in an investigation, and a report made in good faith will never affect your
        participation in the Foundation's community or programs. Reports are handled confidentially
        to the extent possible consistent with a thorough investigation. Read the
        full <a href="/policies/whistleblower/">Whistleblower Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-gap" aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how">How to report</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        The Whistleblower Policy provides three routes, described in Article III. Choose the one
        that fits your situation.
      </p>

      <div class="routes">
        <div class="route">
          <h3>Direct report</h3>
          <p>
            Submit a report in writing to the Chair of the Board of Directors
            at <a href="mailto:chair@openarcollective.org">chair@openarcollective.org</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="route">
          <h3>Reports involving the Chair</h3>
          <p>
            If your concern involves the Chair, send it to the Vice Chair
            at <a href="mailto:vicechair@openarcollective.org">vicechair@openarcollective.org</a> instead.
            The Chair will not see reports sent to this address.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="route">
          <h3>Anonymous report</h3>
          <p>
            To report anonymously, send a written report by postal mail with no return address:
          </p>
          <address>
            The Open Accounts Receivable Collective Foundation<br />
            RE: Whistleblower Report<br />
            3000 S Hulen Street<br />
            Suite 124-735<br />
            Fort Worth, TX 76109
          </address>
          <p>
            Anonymous reports will be investigated to the extent possible given the information
            provided.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="notice" role="note">
        <p>
          <strong>Email is not anonymous.</strong> A report sent to either address above identifies
          your email address to the person who reads it. Postal mail without a return address is
          the anonymous channel. The Foundation does not yet operate an anonymous electronic
          reporting form, and this page will be updated when one is available.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-gap" aria-labelledby="include">
      <h2 id="include">What to include</h2>
      <p>
        Reports should include a description of the conduct giving rise to the concern, the names of
        the people involved if known, relevant dates, and any supporting documentation. A report
        does not need to be exhaustive to trigger an investigation. A good-faith concern is enough.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-gap" aria-labelledby="outside">
      <h2 id="outside">Reporting to outside authorities</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing in the Whistleblower Policy prevents any person from reporting suspected violations
        of law to appropriate governmental authorities, including the Internal Revenue Service,
        state attorneys general, or law enforcement agencies. People who in good faith report
        suspected violations to those authorities are protected under the policy.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section-gap {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .routes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .route {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--c-amber);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: rgba(22, 20, 16, 0.5);
    padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .route h3 {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .route p {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
  }

  .route address {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--c-line);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .notice {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
</style>
